<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n521" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγῑνέω</span></b> , lengthd. 
			Ep.
		 and 
			Ion.
		 (also later 
			Dor.
		, v. sub fin.) form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγω,</span> mostly used in pres. and
		impf. (with or without augm. in <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i>); inf.
		pres.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγινέμεναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					20.213
				</span></i>
			: impf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγίνεσκον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					17.294
				</span></i>
			 (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠγίνεσκον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arat.
					111
				</span></i>
			): fut.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγινήσω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Ap.</u>
					57
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				249
			</span></i>, al.:—<i>lead, bring,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νύμΦας.. ἠγίνεον ἀνὰ ἄστυ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					18.493
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῆλον ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					14.105
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. αἶγας μνηστήρεσσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					22.198
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγίνεον ἄσπετον ὕλην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					24.784
				</span></i>
			; freq. of offerings, dedications, etc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῶρα ἀγίνεον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					3.89
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				93
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				97
			</span></i>, etc., <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Herod.
				4.87
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Iamb.</u>
				1.251
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.75
			</span></i> (Paul. Sil.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλοῦτον ἀ. εἰς ἀρετήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Crates Theb.
					10.8
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ληιάδας ἀ.</span>”
				<i>lead captive,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.613
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνθεα τοσσάπερ ὧραι ποικίλ᾽ ἀγινεῦσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Ap.</u>
					82
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέτρατον ἦμαρ ἀ.,</span> of the
			moon, <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				792
			</span></i>; <i>keep, observe,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παιγνίην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Herod.
					3.55
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, <i>cause to be brought,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς τὸ ἱρὸν ἀγινεόμενος γυναῖκας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.33
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Ind.</u>
				32.7
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἴκα τὰ πάθεα τᾶς ψυχᾶς ἐς τὸ
					μέτριον ἀγινῆται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hippod.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				4.1.94
			</span></i>.</div>
